**Most important finding — Quick start:** I read the SAGE daemon's source (`main.rs`) and it goes further than the visitor reported. The daemon listens on every network interface. Only `/chat`, `/observe` and `/conversations` refuse callers from other machines. `/chat/raw` (direct access to the model), `/stream`, `/delegate` and `/chat/history` accept anyone on the network. The warning now sits above the command that starts the daemon, where before it only came after it. Whether SAGE should listen only on the local machine by default is a question for SAGE itself. I didn't file an issue there because that repo belongs to another track.

